{
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Act 4: The Disguise",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s05b01",
     "shot": "night_flight",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "On the night of 20 June 1791, Louis XVI,",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:1791,",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b02",
     "shot": "escape",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Marie Antoinette and their children slipped out of the Tuileries Palace in Paris,",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       4,
       0.35
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "camp"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b03",
     "shot": "escape",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "the king dressed as a valet, heading for loyal troops near the border.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       4,
       0.35
      ],
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:valet,",
       0.5
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "camp"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b04",
     "shot": "varennes_map",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "They made it most of the way.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "whoosh",
       4,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b05",
     "shot": "varennes_stop",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Then, at a town called Varennes, they were stopped.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       0,
       0.35
      ],
      [
       "slam",
       "w:stopped.",
       0.7
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b06",
     "shot": "banknote",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Stories say a postmaster recognised the king from his portrait on a banknote.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       4,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b07",
     "shot": "banknote",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Historians argue about the details.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:argue",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b08",
     "shot": "march_back",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "They don't argue about the result: the royal family was marched back to Paris in near silence.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [],
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b09",
     "shot": "scales",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "This mattered more than any speech.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b10",
     "shot": "scales",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Until then, most French people wanted a king under a constitution.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:constitution.",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b11",
     "shot": "scales",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "After Varennes, many decided the king had never believed in any of it.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "creak",
       "w:never",
       0.6
      ],
      [
       "thud",
       82,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b12",
     "shot": "scales",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The idea of no king at all stopped being unthinkable.",
     "date": 1791,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:king",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b13",
     "shot": "war",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Then came war.",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:war.",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b14",
     "shot": "war",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In April 1792 France declared war on Austria.",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "clang",
       "w:war",
       0.8
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b15",
     "shot": "manifesto",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "That summer, the commander of the Austrian and Prussian armies threatened Paris with destruction",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       2,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b16",
     "shot": "manifesto",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "if the royal family was harmed.",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       2,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b17",
     "shot": "backfire",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It backfired spectacularly.",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boom",
       "w:backfired",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b18",
     "shot": "tuileries_storm",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "On 10 August 1792 a crowd stormed the Tuileries,",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "rumble",
       0,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b19",
     "shot": "tuileries_storm",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "hundreds of the king's Swiss Guards were killed,",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b20",
     "shot": "tuileries_storm",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "and the monarchy was suspended.",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "thud",
       46,
       0.8
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b21",
     "shot": "republic",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "By September France was a republic.",
     "date": 1792,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:republic.",
       0.6
      ],
      [
       "pops",
       44,
       0.3
      ]
     ],
     "mood": "grand"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b22",
     "shot": "trial",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "At his trial, the king was stripped of his titles and called 'Citizen Louis",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:Citizen",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b23",
     "shot": "trial",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Capet.' There's that name again.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:again.",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b24",
     "shot": "jan21",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "On 21 January 1793 he was guillotined in what is now the Place de la Concorde.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b25",
     "shot": "marie_oct",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Marie Antoinette followed on 16 October.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b26",
     "shot": "marie_oct",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "October again.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b27",
     "shot": "besieged",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "With the king dead, every monarchy in Europe was at war with France,",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       4,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b28",
     "shot": "besieged",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "there were uprisings inside the country, prices were spiralling,",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "rumble",
       "w:uprisings",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b29",
     "shot": "besieged",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "and fear took over.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [],
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b30",
     "shot": "robespierre_intro",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The revolution needed someone to protect it, and it found a small-town lawyer who",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:lawyer",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s05b31",
     "shot": "robespierre_intro",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "didn't drink, didn't gamble, and was nicknamed The Incorruptible.",
     "date": 1793,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "hit",
       "w:drink,",
       0.4
      ],
      [
       "hit",
       "w:gamble,",
       0.4
      ],
      [
